### Component 5: SSE Streaming (`app/main.py`, `core/planner/`)

`POST /plan` streams typed SSE events per graph transition.

#### [MODIFY] `app/main.py`
- `POST /plan` accepts `TripRequest` body, returns `StreamingResponse` with `text/event-stream`.
- Each graph node emits an SSE event on transition: `constraints_parsed`, `retrieving`, `drafting`, `validating`, `violation_found`, `replanning`, `awaiting_approval`, `finalised`, `aborted`.
- Each event carries full payload (current constraints, retrieved venues, draft itinerary, violations, etc.) so the UI can render without extra requests.

#### [NEW] `core/planner/events.py`
- `SSEEvent` Pydantic model: `event_type: str`, `payload: dict`, `timestamp: datetime`.
- `emit_event(event_type, payload) -> SSEEvent`: factory for SSE events.
- Each graph node function is wrapped to emit the corresponding event before/after execution.

